  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>790</x>
      <y>80</y>
      <w>460</w>
      <h>110</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Runs on the JavaFX UI thread. Facade calls that return a
CompletableFuture never block it; results come back through
Platform.runLater(). onStatusChanged() is called on the
indexing worker thread, so it hands updates over the same way.
latestQueryId lets it discard results from outdated searches.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1810</x>
      <y>950</y>
      <w>470</w>
      <h>220</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>The only entry point for the GUI and the CLI.
Methods that return a CompletableFuture start their work on
backgroundExecutor and return immediately. The GUI never waits
on a future; the CLI simply calls join().
Other methods are quick and synchronous. Folder and exclusion
changes are rejected when indexMode is READ_ONLY, because
another process owns the index (see SM01).
modelSettings is the model for new conversations; setBackend()
changes it, and existing conversations keep their own model.
A saved conversation whose model is no longer configured
opens read-only.
Preview and Comparison are simple result records.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>5420</x>
      <y>2220</y>
      <w>350</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Thread-safe: read by the watcher and indexing
threads, and changed from the UI thread.
builtInRules exclude credential locations
(SSH keys, browser profiles, .env files).</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>4410</x>
      <y>2220</y>
      <w>270</w>
      <h>50</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>backendType is CLOUD or LOCAL.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>4310</x>
      <y>2620</y>
      <w>460</w>
      <h>260</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>One entry per chunk of each indexed file, stored together
with that file's attributes (path, type, size, modified time).
So filters are applied inside the query, including vector
search; a removed file disappears from results immediately;
and two copies of a file are two separate results.
remove(path) on a folder removes every file under it.
addEmbeddings() updates every file with that content.

open() takes the index's write lock if it can (mode WRITER);
otherwise it opens the index READ_ONLY ("first process wins").
Single writer: only the indexing worker thread calls put(),
addEmbeddings(), remove(), and commit(). Reads are safe from
any thread and see the last refreshed snapshot. A READ_ONLY
process calls refresh() every few seconds.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3620</x>
      <y>2220</y>
      <w>470</w>
      <h>140</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Keyed by content hash and never searched: it exists only so
content that was already extracted and embedded can be reused.
A renamed, moved, restored, or copied file copies its chunks
and embeddings from here instead of being processed again.
Removing a file doesn't touch it; pruneUnreferenced() deletes
content that no indexed file has used for maxAge.
Only the indexing worker thread uses it.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>5440</x>
      <y>2820</y>
      <w>310</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>extractionStatus is OK, PARTIAL,
METADATA_ONLY, NO_TEXT, or FAILED.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>5840</x>
      <y>3150</y>
      <w>300</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>embedding stays empty until the second
indexing phase fills it in (see SD01).</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>4360</x>
      <y>5420</y>
      <w>370</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Must be thread-safe: the indexing worker embeds
chunks while background threads embed queries.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3660</x>
      <y>5560</y>
      <w>380</w>
      <h>80</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Adapts an embedding model that runs inside the
application's process (for example, an ONNX model
run through LangChain4j) to EmbeddingModel.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2790</x>
      <y>2500</y>
      <w>390</w>
      <h>140</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Watches each search folder recursively, including
subfolders created later, on its own watcher thread.
For each change it offers the path to ChangeQueue if
IndexConfig includes it; when the operating system
reports lost events (overflow), it offers the whole
search folder instead. A rename arrives as a delete
plus a create; ContentStore makes that cheap.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3630</x>
      <y>2400</y>
      <w>440</w>
      <h>140</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Thread-safe. offer() is called from the watcher thread and
records the latest change time for each path, so a burst of
events for one file becomes a single entry.
takeReady() is called by the indexing worker. It returns a path
only once it has been unchanged for quietPeriod (about 2 s),
or null when nothing is ready before the timeout.
A folder in the queue means "rescan this folder".</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2740</x>
      <y>3500</y>
      <w>500</w>
      <h>220</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Only started in WRITER mode. Its worker thread is the only
writer of SearchIndex and ContentStore. requestUpdate() only
offers a path to the queue, so it returns immediately and is
safe from any thread.
Phase 1, indexFile(), makes a file keyword-searchable. If
ContentStore already has its content, the stored chunks and
embeddings are copied instead of extracting again.
Phase 2, embedNextBatch(), embeds content that has no embeddings
yet when no file is ready, and prunes ContentStore when there
is nothing to embed.
Status listeners are called on the worker thread.
state takes the values of the states in SM01.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3650</x>
      <y>2590</y>
      <w>410</w>
      <h>190</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Detects the file type from the file's contents and
returns its text page by page, with its type and
metadata (an ExtractedDocument).
Must not be able to crash or hang the application:
parsing runs isolated from the app's process, with a
time limit and a memory limit.
Throws UnsupportedFormatException for formats it can't
read, an IOException if the file is locked, and
ExtractionException if the file is corrupt or
password-protected, or parsing hit a limit or crashed.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2800</x>
      <y>2680</y>
      <w>370</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Adapts a document-parsing library that can run
in a separate process (for example, Apache Tika's
forked parser) to TextExtractor. The rest of the
system never sees the library's types.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3710</x>
      <y>2820</y>
      <w>280</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Splits each page separately, so every
chunk keeps its page number.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3640</x>
      <y>4520</y>
      <w>420</w>
      <h>180</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Safe to call from several background threads at once:
it only reads the index. fuseRankings() merges keyword
and semantic hits by rank (reciprocal rank fusion).
If the embedding model is unavailable, or the CLI gets
--keyword-only, semanticSearchEnabled is false and only
keyword hits are used. The ranked ChunkHits are grouped
by file path into SearchResults, so copies of a file are
separate results.
Each DiffHunk in a DiffResult is one changed region.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2780</x>
      <y>5220</y>
      <w>420</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>run() blocks until the answer is ready, so it is only
called on a background thread (see FindAnythingService).
Holds no model client: each call is given the client to
use, so a conversation always talks to its own model.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3660</x>
      <y>6820</y>
      <w>390</w>
      <h>110</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Bound to one model for its whole life (modelSettings,
set when it is created), so text never moves from a
local model's conversation to a cloud model.
Used by one request at a time: the GUI disables
Ask mode input while a request is running.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>4990</x>
      <y>5940</y>
      <w>250</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>status is VERIFIED, UNVERIFIED,
or SOURCE_CHANGED.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2780</x>
      <y>6920</y>
      <w>410</w>
      <h>130</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Adapts a LangChain4j ChatModel (Anthropic for cloud,
Ollama for local) to LlmClient, converting LlmRequest
and LlmResponse to and from the library's message and
tool types. The rest of the system never sees library
types. Clients keep no state between calls, so they
are thread-safe.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2790</x>
      <y>6820</y>
      <w>390</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Returns one cached client per ModelSettings: the
decorated chain for CLOUD, a plain client for LOCAL.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>4350</x>
      <y>7140</y>
      <w>390</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>A Message has a role (user, assistant, or tool), its
content, and the source files the content came from,
which RedactingLlmClient uses to withhold local-only
content. A ToolCall names a tool and its arguments.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3670</x>
      <y>1470</y>
      <w>370</w>
      <h>80</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>One implementation per category: card numbers
and SINs (both checked with the Luhn checksum),
private keys, and API keys.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2820</x>
      <y>1640</y>
      <w>340</w>
      <h>80</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Redactor, FolderPolicy, and PrivacyLog are
thread-safe: background request threads use
them while the UI thread changes them.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
